{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1050,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we think of looking for extra-terrestrial\nlife, we tend to focus on “earth-like”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4920,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "planets, that is, planets with conditions\nthat are similar to our own. “Life exists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9140,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on earth,” the logic goes, “so earth-like\nconditions are probably a good bet to find"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13670,
    "dDurationMs": 1030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more life.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14700,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15700,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are hundreds of billions of galaxies\nin the observable universe, each with billions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19550,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if not trillions of stars, and most stars\nhave planets orbiting them. That’s roughly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24300,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a million billion billion planets. The enormity\nof this number means it’s probably safe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28740,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to assume that there are many many *many*\nother planets with life - even intelligent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33300,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34300,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this, together with some basic physics\nand fancy statistics, implies it’s more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38190,
    "dDurationMs": 4529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "likely that species of intelligent extraterrestrials\nwill live on habitable planets unlike earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42719,
    "dDurationMs": 4741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and will be unlike humans. More precisely,\nthey’ll be bigger than us and live in smaller"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47460,
    "dDurationMs": 1649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "groups on smaller planets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49109,
    "dDurationMs": 4811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, I know it sounds crazy that with only\none data point – us – we can make any"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53920,
    "dDurationMs": 4529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "predictions at all about aliens we don’t\neven know exist. But we can – here’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58449,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59449,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A basic result in statistics is that there’s\na big difference between the properties of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63039,
    "dDurationMs": 4031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a typical *individual* and the properties\nof an individual in a typical *group*. The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67070,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "majority of humans, for example, live in countries\nwith a population of at least 180 million"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71680,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people. But the majority of countries have\npopulations of less than 6 million."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75710,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the majority of *religious* humans are\nmembers of religions with more than a billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79650,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "followers, while the majority of *religions*\nhave fewer than a million followers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83700,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the majority of people who follow the\nEnglish Premier league are fans of teams with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87540,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hundreds of millions of fans like Manchester\nUnited, while most *teams* have just a few"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92110,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "million fans each."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93350,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It doesn’t matter how many individuals you\nhave, or how you make the groups – they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97310,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can be religions, or fans of sports teams,\nor the ingredients of this trail mix. It is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102130,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a mathematical fact that the group that the\nmedian individual belongs to will be at least"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106570,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as big/bigger than the median group. Or, simply\nput, any time groups are not all the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110920,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "size, most individuals will be members of\ngroups that are bigger than most of the other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115380,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "groups."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116380,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The takeaway is that an individual should\nexpect to be a member of a large group, not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119600,
    "dDurationMs": 3831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an ordinary one. If you don’t know what\ngroup you fall into (like, I don’t know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123431,
    "dDurationMs": 4239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what my blood type is), the most likely groups\nto be in are the biggest ones – I’m probably"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127670,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "O or A positive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129260,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when it comes to intelligent life forms,\nwe humans don’t know what kind of group"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132950,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we fall into. So statistics tells us that\nwe, as individuals, should expect to be members"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137570,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a large group of intelligent beings. That\nis, we should expect that our species has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141510,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a higher population than most other species.\nAnd just knowing that we probably have a high"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145700,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "population tells us a lot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148090,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, individual living beings require\nspace to live – I mean, the countries with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152480,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the biggest populations tend to have large\nland areas – so earth, with its high population,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156980,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is probably bigger than most other planets\nwith intelligent life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160300,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, smaller living creatures need less\nspace and energy per creature, and accordingly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164940,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tend to have higher population densities:\nthat’s why there are way more ants on earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168830,
    "dDurationMs": 5310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than elephants. So humans, with our high population,\nare probably physically smaller than most"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174140,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other species of intelligent life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175710,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, we should expect to be abnormal among\nintelligent aliens when it comes to anything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179940,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that influences overall population size. Like,\neasily available energy makes it easier to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184650,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maintain higher populations, so we should\nexpect our sun to be somewhat hotter and brighter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188570,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and closer than the stars of most intelligent\nalien species; and we should expect our atmosphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193150,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be more transparent to our star’s light;\nand so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195400,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If this all sounds a bit unspecific, well,\nwith just a few more simple and reasonable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199340,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assumptions based on basic physics, we can\nbe more precise. Researchers have predicted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203590,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the population of most intelligent alien\nspecies should be below 20 million individuals;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208280,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the majority of planets with intelligent life\nshould have less than 80% the radius of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212390,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "earth; and the individuals of most intelligent\nalien species should be at least as massive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216080,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as polar bears."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217540,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead of looking for nearby intelligent\nextraterrestrials on “earth-like planets”,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221640,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the intelligent approach might be to look\nfor habitable planets slightly smaller, darker,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226500,
    "dDurationMs": 27670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hazier than our own. In short, we should\nexpect to be the Manchester United "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254170,
    "dDurationMs": 8149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the universe, searching for AFC Wimbledon."
    } ]
  } ]
}
